---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getApp, COMPANY } from '../../data/apps';

const app = getApp('pulsewire')!;
const lastUpdated = 'August 21, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${app.name} Privacy Policy — ${COMPANY.name}`}
  description="How PulseWire handles private account, reading, story, AI, and offline Saved data."
  path={`/${app.slug}/privacy`}
  noindex={true}
  socialImage="/apps/pulsewire.png"
  socialImageAlt="PulseWire app icon"
>
  <article class="prose container">
    <a class="back-link" href="/pulsewire">← {app.name}</a>
    <h1>{app.name} Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      This policy explains how {COMPANY.name} (“we”, “us”) handles information
      in {app.name}, a private, single-owner story-intelligence reader. The
      production workspace is access-controlled and is not exposed from the
      portfolio as a public reader or demo.
    </p>

    <h2>Information the service processes</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Account information.</strong> Microsoft Entra ID provides the
        stable account identifier and basic profile claims needed to create and
        secure the allowed session. Access is restricted to configured
        principals.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sources and reading activity.</strong> PulseWire stores selected
        feed subscriptions, source records, story groupings, chronology,
        evidence and review state, Saved stories, and read state needed to
        operate the reader.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Generated analysis.</strong> Briefs, embeddings, ranking inputs,
        and related model output are stored where needed to build and explain
        the private edition.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Operational records.</strong> Authentication-session state,
        worker and feed health, request timing, version information, and errors
        are processed to secure, run, recover, and troubleshoot the service.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      PulseWire does not use third-party advertising or cross-app tracking and
      does not need precise location, contacts, or advertising identifiers.
    </p>

    <h2>Server storage</h2>
    <p>
      PulseWire uses PostgreSQL on Microsoft Azure. The database includes
      pgvector data used for story and source retrieval. This is a private
      single-owner service, not a claim that every record lives in a separate
      per-user database. Information is encrypted in transit using HTTPS, and
      service access is limited to what is needed to operate and secure the
      workspace.
    </p>

    <h2>AI processing</h2>
    <p>
      PulseWire uses configured Azure AI services to generate briefs and
      embeddings from source material and story context. The service sends the
      content required for that operation and stores the resulting analysis
      needed by the reader. Provider processing is governed by the applicable
      service terms; this policy does not promise legal or technical controls
      beyond the configuration actually deployed.
    </p>

    <h2>Offline Saved snapshots</h2>
    <p>
      The installable web app can explicitly download a Saved story snapshot
      for offline reading. That local copy may include the story text, source
      evidence, and presentation data needed to read it. PulseWire does not
      silently download the whole workspace and does not represent this
      server-backed reader as local-first.
    </p>
    <p>
      Offline data remains in the browser profile until it is removed by the
      app, the browser, the operating system, or the person controlling that
      profile. Anyone with access to the profile may be able to read local
      copies. Remove Saved downloads before sharing or disposing of a device.
    </p>

    <h2>Sharing and service providers</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell personal information. Microsoft provides identity, Azure
      hosts the application and database, and configured AI services process
      content needed for generated analysis. Information may also be disclosed
      where required by law or needed to protect the service.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      Server records are retained while the private workspace is active and as
      needed for recovery, security, or legal obligations. Offline Saved copies
      follow the browser-storage behavior above. To request access to or
      deletion of account-associated data, email
      <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is intended for a general, adult audience and is not directed
      to children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from
      children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy when the service or its data practices change.
      The “Last updated” date above identifies the current version.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or your data? Email
      <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
